prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a 3D chess game. Load ABeautifulGame.glb (containing the complete chessboard and pieces) and implement basic piece-movement interactions.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/ABeautifulGame.glb;
(2) The model contains the chessboard and all pieces and must be displayed centered;

[Piece Mapping]
(3) Traverse the model's child meshes and map the pieces to the 8x8 chessboard squares based on their names or positions;
(4) Distinguish the white and black pieces (by material color or name);

[Piece-Movement Interaction]
(5) Use a Raycaster to detect clicks on pieces;
(6) On the first click, select a piece (highlight it with a yellow emissive color) and display its available destination squares (green translucent blocks);
(7) On the second click, execute the move to the target square: smoothly animate the piece moving to the target position;
(8) If the target square contains an opponent's piece, "capture" it (remove it from the scene);

[Turn-Based Play]
(9) White moves first, and turns alternate;
(10) Only the current side's own pieces may be moved;

[Basic Rules (Simplified)]
(11) Implement only simple move validation: the square must be within the chessboard bounds, and the target square must not contain a piece belonging to the current side;
(12) Full rules (such as check, special pawn moves, etc.) do not need to be implemented, but movement directions must be basically correct;

[OrbitControls]
(13) Support rotating the view around the chessboard;

[HUD Display]
(14) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Current side to move (id="currentTurn", "White"/"Black")
  - Move count (id="moveCount")
  - Number of captured pieces (id="capturedCount")
  - Selected piece (id="selectedPiece")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ on every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - currentTurn: string ("white"/"black")
  - moveCount: number
  - capturedCount: number
  - selectedPiece: string (name of the selected piece; "" indicates none)
  - boardState: Array (8x8 array of strings representing the simplified board state)

Output a single standalone HTML file.
